  "summary_en": "Louisiana Act 214 (SB 147, 2021) creates a statutory framework for personal delivery devices, sidewalk delivery robots with automated driving under remote human supervision. It sets operator duties, speed and area limits, equipment and identification requirements, local prohibition powers, and mandatory $100,000 liability insurance.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Only business entities with a trained agent monitoring or controlling the device may operate PDDs; the entity is the operator for traffic-law purposes.",
   "PDDs must yield to pedestrians and traffic, and may travel up to 12 mph in pedestrian areas and 20 mph in nonpedestrian areas.",
   "Devices need an identification marker with owner contact and unique ID, a braking system, and lights at night.",
   "Local governments and airports may prohibit PDDs in the interest of public safety.",
   "Operators must carry at least $100,000 general liability insurance."
  ],
